# ReciFinder - Project Walkthrough

The **ReciFinder** mobile application has been successfully created. It is a complete Flutter project that interacts with the public TheMealDB API, uses Provider for robust state management, and features a clean, responsive, and aesthetically pleasing modern UI.

## Changes Made

- **Project Scaffolding**: Initialized `recifinder` Flutter project in `C:\Users\Lenovo\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\recifinder` and updated `pubspec.yaml` with the required dependencies (`http`, `provider`, `cached_network_image`, `google_fonts`).
- **Data Model**: Implemented `[meal.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/models/meal.dart)` for parsing the sophisticated JSON response from TheMealDB, including robust extraction of dynamic ingredient lists.
- **Network Layer**: Built `[api_service.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/services/api_service.dart)` to handle REST API calls to search for meals by name and lookup complete meal details by ID.
- **State Management**: Created `[recipe_provider.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/providers/recipe_provider.dart)` implementing `ChangeNotifier` to seamlessly manage search results, loading states, and error handling.
- **UI Components**:
  - `[recipe_card.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/widgets/recipe_card.dart)`: Developed a reusable, visually appealing card widget utilizing `CachedNetworkImage` with placeholder/error handling to display summarized recipe information.
  - `[home_screen.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/screens/home_screen.dart)`: Implemented the main search interface featuring a pristine input layout, automatic loading of predefined queries (e.g., 'chicken'), pull-to-refresh capabilities, and robust blank/error state handlers.
  - `[recipe_detail_screen.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/screens/recipe_detail_screen.dart)`: Created an immersive detail view utilizing `CustomScrollView` and `SliverAppBar` with Hero transitions to cleanly display ingredients, measurements, and cooking instructions.
- **App Configuration**: Integrated sophisticated Google Fonts (`Outfit`) into the Material 3 app theme in `[main.dart](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/recifinder/lib/main.dart)`, and injected the global `RecipeProvider`.

## How to Run & Build

To run the application locally on an attached device or emulator, navigate to the project directory in your terminal and execute:
```bash
cd C:\Users\Lenovo\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\recifinder
flutter run
```

### Build APK (for direct Android installation)

To build a release APK, execute the following command:
```bash
cd C:\Users\Lenovo\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\recifinder
flutter build apk --release
```
*The resulting APK will be located at `build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk`*

### Build App Bundle (AAB) (for Google Play Store)

To build a release App Bundle, execute the following command:
```bash
cd C:\Users\Lenovo\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\recifinder
flutter build appbundle
```
*The resulting AAB will be located at `build/app/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab`*

## Validation Results

The application's compilation status and syntax correctness were successfully validated by building a release APK in the underlying system background, resulting in zero compilation or dependency resolution errors.
